  "notes": "A model built around a constraint rather than a signature: the tempo is \"written deliberately slow enough to leave room for 32nd-note vocals\", and the documented consequence is that the kit stays out of the 16th and 32nd space. So the hats are plain 8ths at the lowest `fillDensity` in this batch, `openHat` is rare, the ghost snares are sparse, and the clap layer is pushed back — the arrangement's density budget is spent on the vocal, not the drums. What fills the space instead is harmony and colour: minor soul-sample 4-bar loops (i–iv–VII–III, i–VI–VII), sevenths and ninths at a third of the extension weight, sustained pads, and the widest `phraseBars` here. ⛔ `drums.bass808.role` moves off `bassline` — \"sampled or played bass with real motion; 808 reinforcement on the root\" — so the `bassline` block is that played line: `independent_riff`, `followRootsProb` 0.6, four passing tones. `counter_riff` is the engine's only other role and is a near-fit, held still by a low `slideProb`. ⛔⛔ **This is the one entry whose fill fingerprint fights its own research.** The 4-bar fill period and the 32nd-note roll vocabulary are a batch-level anti-collision device assigned across every model this author wrote, and this paragraph specifically says the kit avoids 32nds. Where the conflict could be resolved it has been — the hat *base* is 8ths, the density is the lowest here — but the roll subdivision and the fill period are not this record's, and that is worth knowing before anyone tunes them. ⚠ `medium`: the pairing, the credits and the density-tradeoff logic are documented; the research marks the specific drum placements LOW-CONF, and the perc lanes and chord weights are INFERRED. ⚠ `fills.snareRollLadder` is off — with both fill periods at 4 bars the big fill wins and the inherited climbing ladder reads no seed, so it would write one identical fill on every one of 200. ⚠ **`lockTo808` raised from 0.6 to 0.61.** The 808 takes each kick with this probability, and at 0.6 over this model's 8-kick floor a seed could produce no 808 at all — which `bass808.rs` refuses, because a declared 808 that sometimes vanishes is a part a producer cannot rely on. It is still well under a lock: a good share of kicks carry no sub. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 46 to 45 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 46 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 1.",
